WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.140
This is the story

c2
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.280
of A checkout slowdown,

c3
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.100
from the postmortem.

c4
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.640
14:02 UTC.

c5
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.500
Deploy 2.3 rolled out.

c6
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.030
14:05 UTC.

c7
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.270
Checkout requests start

c8
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:12.930
timing out.

c9
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.900
14:09 UTC.

c10
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.760
Error rate above 5%.

c11
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.260
14:17 UTC.

c12
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.180
On-call starts a rollback.

c13
00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:24.655
14:31 UTC.

c14
00:00:24.655 --> 00:00:25.695
Rollback finished,

c15
00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:27.355
errors back to normal.

c16
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:28.820
It took 4 minutes

c17
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.780
from the first failure

c18
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.220
to the alert.

c19
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.690
It took 26 minutes

c20
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:33.610
from the first failure

c21
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.950
to the fix.
